```c
else if (strcmp(vid_renderer->string, "gl3") == 0)
{
    Com_Printf("Retrying with gles3...\n");
    Cvar_Set("vid_renderer", "gles");
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when the current renderer is "gl3", the code incorrectly sets the renderer to "gles" instead of the intended "gles3". This misconfiguration can lead to improper rendering behavior as the application expects to use the OpenGL ES 3 renderer but instead uses the OpenGL ES 2 renderer.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
else if (strcmp(vid_renderer->string, "gl3") == 0)
{
    Com_Printf("Retrying with gles3...\n");
    Cvar_Set("vid_renderer", "gles3");
}
```
Reason:
The fix changes the renderer setting from "gles" to "gles3" when the current renderer is "gl3". This ensures that the application correctly attempts to use the intended OpenGL ES 3 renderer, thereby resolving the improper rendering behavior caused by the previous misconfiguration.

